# Complexity Comparison

| Approach                                                  | Time Complexity                                                           | Space Complexity | Works for Constraints? |
| --------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------- | ---------------------- |
| Brute Force                                               | (O(n^2 \log n)) (plus GCD computations)                                   | (O(n^2))         | ❌ No                   |
| Optimal (Frequency + Inclusion-Exclusion + Binary Search) | (O(M \log M + Q \log M)), where (M = \max(\text{nums}) \le 5 \times 10^4) | (O(M))           | ✅ Yes                  |

Here, (M) is the maximum value in `nums`, and the harmonic-series sum of iterating over multiples gives the (O(M \log M)) behavior. This makes the solution efficient for the given limits.
